monster hunter rise is the latest and  greatest in the monster hunter series  it streamlines some of the pre-existing  systems and adds a gigaton of new  features like new ways to get around  a writable dog friend called a palamoot  a new endemic life form called a wire  bug which increases your mobility in the  world your dexterity and fights and it  adds a new skill for each of the 14  weapon types  but we're here to talk shop on the  tetranodon so let's jump right into it  the tetranodon is based on a water demon  from japanese folklore called a kappa  who in stories loves sumo wrestling  and steals your organs through your butt  in monster hunter rise though the only  thing that tetranodon does to your butt  has beat the hell  out of it but that is bad enough so when  you go up against one you'll need to be  prepared  as they say knowledge is half the battle  so let's study our big fat water  dwelling enemy  tetranodon has two states in the first  smaller milder form it walks around on  four legs so its movement speed is  increased but its size and damage are  smaller compared to its larger form  big t gorges itself on gravel or pond  scum or something when it senses a fight  coming  expanding its size and weight and it  adds a massive increase in damage  each of the forms come with their own  attack patterns or variations so you'll  need to change your approach after your  prey is eaten  when in its natural state the tetronodon  has a straightforward rush attack you'll  need to sideways dodge to avoid the  expanded version of this attack will be  harder to dodge because it cuts a much  wider path the tetranodon can spit water  with its water breath attack in both of  its forms  the super-sized version of this delivers  a single stream of water with increased  damage  this big dude can pick up a boulder and  throw it at you  as soon as you see the tetranodon go for  a rock it's best to stand back  watch its movements and wait for the  toss so you can see where it's going to  land and get out of the way  despite its large size this thing can  move its jump attack will launch the  tatranodon into the air and when it  lands you better not be there  it has a massive area of effect and huge  damage in the expanded form  being based on a sumo wrestling yokai  the tetranodon has a foot slam attack  which shoots out sideways from its body  the large version of this attack causes  tremor but can be dodged  using the wire bug i mentioned before so  how do you prepare your hunter for this  battle  health potions to take the edge off the  damage you're definitely going to take  no buries to remove some of the status  effects like water blight  dung bombs to stun him if he tries to  eat you and possibly some trimmer  resistance to your armor  gathering endemic life can be a massive  help as well the cloth fly can distract  as well as boost your defense  and like many other monsters the  tetranodon is territorial  so use the whale nard to attract other  monsters to provoke a fight which will  be both  entertaining and take some of the  tetranodon's health during the fight  focus on the tatranodon's head front  legs and exposed belly to do the most  damage  once the aquatic demon is defeated you  can use his carpus  hide head disc and beak to create new  armor which increases defense  as well as water and ice resistance or  new weapons that add water  damage to your arsenal of oversized  monster killing devices  monster hunter rises out on nintendo  switch on march 26th  i'll see you in the new rampage mode  shall we go
 

